  "summary": "Experience the simple elegance of traditional Mediterranean home cooking with this comforting <b>Greek lentil soup</b>. Known locally as Fakes, this hearty <b>vegetarian soup</b> relies on wholesome brown lentils cooked alongside sweet carrots, celery, and onions in a rich herbal broth. Tomato paste adds color and depth, while bay leaves and dried oregano infuse the pot with classical Aegean flavors. A key finishing step involves stirring in a splash of red wine vinegar and raw extra virgin olive oil just before serving, which brightens the savory earthiness of the pulses. High in fiber and plant-based protein, this nutritious dish is both budget-friendly and remarkably easy to prepare on busy weeknights. Serve it steaming hot alongside crusty sourdough bread, salty feta cheese, and kalamata olives for a authentic Greek dining experience at home. This comforting bowl proves that simple plant-based ingredients can create deeply satisfying meals.",
